WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:05.630
in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:12.670
The reading from the Sinaxadion, per September 5th, on which we commemorate

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:19.070
the Holy Hyromarter Athanasius, abbot of the monastery of Saint Simeon the

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:22.910
Stylite at Brest-Litovsk.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:29.550
Saint Athanasius was born in the province of Minsk in the year 1596.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:37.150
The same year as the false union of Brest-Litovsk was concluded between Rome and some Russian

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:45.630
bishops. His father was a Lithuanian nobleman of modest means, but Athanasius acquired

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:50.030
breath and depth of learning that were exceptional at that time.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:56.190
Besides modern and ancient languages and the writings of the Holy Fathers,

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:00.910
he was familiar with the works of Western philosophers and theologians.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:09.630
In the year 1627, after spending several years as a private tutor, he became a monk

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.670
at the monastery of Kuthin near Orshah in Little Russia.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:23.470
This monastery was independent of the Polish occupying forces, and by tradition deeply

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:30.030
committed to the preservation of Orthodoxy so that it was able to offer great encouragement

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.590
to the Orthodox people in the face of Roman Catholic propaganda.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:42.750
Athanasius went on to follow his monastic path in other renowned monasteries, and was ordained

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:51.790
priest. The Metropolitan of Kiev, Peter Mogila, gave him the task of restoring the monastery of

00:01:51.790 --> 00:02:01.150
Kupiatiks. In obedience to a divine revelation, Athanasius set out for Moscow, a long and dangerous

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:08.830
journey through territory under Polish occupation, in order to ask for financial assistance for the

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:16.830
restoration and to acquaint the Tsar with the fate intended for the Orthodox Church in the lands

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:25.470
to the southwest of Russia. He was successful in his quest, and with the help of the mother of God,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:32.750
the restoration works were begun. Two years later, Athanasius was appointed abbot of the

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:40.910
monastery of St. Simeon the Stylite in Brecht-Litovsk. From then on, he went to be a resolute

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:49.870
and tireless fighter against Roman proselytism clothed in Orthodox rites and customs known as the

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:58.830
Unia. For the next eight years, by prayer, preaching and through his writings, the saint devoted

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:05.950
all his strength to refuting the false union, and to bringing back to the holy sheepfold of Christ,

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:12.590
those who had strayed. The population of the occupied territories was brutally treated by the

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:19.790
Polish soldiers and colonists, nor did the Jesuit missionaries for their part abstain from any measure

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:28.510
that might serve to lead the peoples of Little Russia to accept their faith. In this situation,

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:36.990
Saint Athanasius decided to petition the king of Poland, Vladislav IV, that the Orthodox be treated

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:45.950
with more humanity. The king was moved by his request and issued a decree for bidding the abuses

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:53.550
that had occurred, but his officials ignored it. The condition of the Orthodox in Warsaw was

00:03:53.550 --> 00:04:01.950
particularly bad. It was not unknown for the Poles and Uniaz to set fire to Orthodox churches

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:09.630
on feast days when they were full of the faithful, just as had happened in the time of the great

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:18.750
persecutions. Athanasius kept up the fight, aided, and comforted by none but the mother of God,

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:29.550
and in the year 1643 following a new revelation, he again appealed for redress on behalf

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:37.470
of the Orthodox to the Polish Council of State. He received a favorable hearing, and the Orthodox

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:46.110
were granted some legal protection. But certain Orthodox men of rank, fearing for their privileges,

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:52.270
claimed that the saint was mad and succeeded in having him deprived of his abyssey,

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:59.790
deposed from the priesthood and sent to Kiev to answer before a church court.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:06.750
The humble Athanasius was completely exonerated and restored to his position,

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:15.870
but he did not have peace for long. Since persecution of the Orthodox soon began again.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:24.270
He drew up a petition intended for the king of Poland, but was arrested and thrown into prison

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:30.590
before he was able to complete it. He was released after three years' detention,

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:39.710
but in the year 1648 a persecution broke out that was more terrible than ever before.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:48.670
So bloody was it that the people of little Russia rose up and demanded the departure of the Polish

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:56.670
Lithuanian army and the restoration of Russian territory to the Tsar. The Polish authorities

00:05:56.670 --> 00:06:02.350
immediately arrested the rebel leaders and prominent Orthodox dignitaries.

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:11.150
Saint Athanasius was imprisoned, an endured physical and mental torment of all kinds at the hands

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:20.910
of his jailers and of the Roman Catholic authorities, but he never ceased to cry, a nathema to the union.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:28.670
After being tortured with red-hot calls, he was flayed and burnt alive.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:38.750
As he was still not dead, his executioners shot him. They threw his decapitated corpse into a pit

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:48.110
where it was found some time later, incorrupt. In the years that followed, the relics of the Holy

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:57.870
martyr worked many miracles. Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord, Jesus Christ, our

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:07.550
God, have mercy on us and save us.
